From: Olegd5g56 <47363609+Olegd5g56@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:01:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mfsrcsnk: Deliver queued samples before end of stream.

0009-fix-for-arcania-games-video-playback removed list_empty(&stream->samples)
from media_source_send_eos(). When the demuxer reaches the end of the file,
every active stream then gets MEEndOfStream at once, even with samples still
queued, and media_stream_RequestSample() returns MF_E_END_OF_STREAM from
then on: the tail of a two-track movie is never delivered.

Metro Awakening (2669410) waits for the end of its intro movies on the first
launch and stays on a black screen after the animated logo (#993).

Restore the check, as in upstream wine. With demux_eos set,
media_source_request_stream_sample() still calls media_source_send_eos()
after each sample it delivers, so the EOS follows the last queued sample.

Ported from https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/993
by GloriousEggroll.
---
--- a/dlls/mfsrcsnk/media_source.c
+++ b/dlls/mfsrcsnk/media_source.c
@@ -771,7 +771,7 @@
     PROPVARIANT empty = {.vt = VT_EMPTY};
     UINT i;
 
-    if (stream->active && !stream->eos)
+    if (stream->active && !stream->eos && list_empty(&stream->samples))
     {
         WARN("Queueing MEEndOfStream for stream %p, queued samples %u.\n",
                 stream, list_count(&stream->samples));
